# Step 7 (optional): Train and serve a model

If your product includes a model you train yourself, moving only the agent onto Databricks leaves the most important asset outside your governance. In this step you train a **cancellation-risk** classifier on `samples.wanderbricks`, register it in **Unity Catalog** and serve it on **Model Serving**.

## 7.1 Run the notebook

1. In the workspace, click **Workspace** > your user folder > **Import**, and import `step7-train-serve/train_cancellation_model.py` from the lab files.
2. Open the notebook and connect it to **Serverless** compute.
3. Set the widgets: **catalog** to your catalog, **schema** to `{{ n.schema }}`, **endpoint** to `{{ n.endpoint }}`.
4. Click **Run all**.
5. Verify the notebook:
    - writes the feature table `<catalog>.{{ n.schema }}.booking_features`,
    - prints the test AUC and registers `<catalog>.{{ n.schema }}.cancellation_risk`,
    - sets the alias `champion` and creates the endpoint `{{ n.endpoint }}` with scale to zero,
    - prints predictions for two test bookings in the last cell.

Creating the endpoint takes several minutes.

## 7.2 Check what Unity Catalog recorded

1. Open `<catalog>.{{ n.schema }}.cancellation_risk` in **Catalog Explorer**. Verify the version has the alias `champion` and links to the MLflow run with its parameters and AUC.
2. Click **Lineage** and verify the model traces back through `booking_features` to `samples.wanderbricks.bookings` and `users`.
3. Open **Serving** and verify `{{ n.endpoint }}` serves that version and scales to zero when idle.

## 7.3 (Optional) Give Wanda the model as a tool

To let Wanda warn guests about bookings at risk, add a function tool in `wanda-agent/agent/tools/` that calls the endpoint with the Databricks SDK, `WorkspaceClient().serving_endpoints.query(name="{{ n.endpoint }}", dataframe_records=[...])`, then redeploy. The app's service principal needs **Can Query** on the endpoint.

!!! note "Partly verified"
    The notebook ran end to end on the test workspace. The agent tool in 7.3 is a pattern from the docs and was not tested in this lab.

